XDesk: MIT-SHM's CloseScreen freed its screen private but left pScreen->DestroyPixmap pointing at
ShmDestroyPixmap. A pixmap destroyed later in the close chain (glamor_close_screen frees its glyph
atlases) then read the freed private (NULL + 0x10: destroyPixmap) and the X server crashed on every
stop after text had been drawn. Give the slot back to the procedure it wrapped, as CloseScreen is.
--- a/Xext/shm.c
+++ b/Xext/shm.c
@@ -199,6 +199,9 @@
     ShmScrPrivateRec *screen_priv = ShmGetScreenPriv(pScreen);
 
     pScreen->CloseScreen = screen_priv->CloseScreen;
+    /* XDesk: unwrap DestroyPixmap too, or later pixmaps reach the freed private */
+    if (pScreen->DestroyPixmap == ShmDestroyPixmap)
+        pScreen->DestroyPixmap = screen_priv->destroyPixmap;
     dixSetPrivate(&pScreen->devPrivates, shmScrPrivateKey, NULL);
     free(screen_priv);
     return (*pScreen->CloseScreen) (pScreen);
